WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.107
Claim Assistant turns filled claim
forms into structured, validated data.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.635
Before, staff re-keyed
each claim form by hand.

3
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.584
About 107,000 claims
a year, with 30 staff.

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.742
Intake ran 12 hours
a day, on weekdays only.

5
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.495
Claim Assistant works in 3 steps.

6
00:00:18.495 --> 00:00:20.817
It reads each field, with a confidence.

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.488
It checks the claim against
its policy record.

8
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:27.892
And fields below 80% confidence
go to a person for review.

9
00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.647
Here is a handwritten Florida claim form.

10
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.108
54 fields are read,
and 31 are flagged as low confidence.

11
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:41.675
Checked against the policy, the coverage
call is uncertain.

12
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.341
It writes out why: a likely match,
but not verified with high certainty.

13
00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.621
Every value links back to where
it was read on the form.

14
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.310
The loss description
is traced the same way.

15
00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.173
Here, the company name was read
from the wrong line, at 36%.

16
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.964
A person corrects
it and approves it: 100%.

17
00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:11.898
Once all 31 flagged fields
are reviewed, export unlocks.

18
00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:15.431
The claim is ready for export.

19
00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:18.624
People handle only
the exceptions that need a human.

20
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.493
Claim Assistant.

21
00:01:21.493 --> 00:01:25.225
Staff review the exceptions, instead
of re-keying every claim.
